ld -Clinker-flavor=ld64.lld, a full vendored offline cargo build produced a running Mach-O arm64 executable with ZERO PATH-resolved executables (poisoned-PATH shim probe, 20 names, 0 hits); the red control without those pins resolved xcrun and cc from PATH. Process closure is therefore cargo->rustc->rust-lld, entirely inside the fingerprinted Rust root; the macOS SDK is a data-only second fingerprinted root (261MB, 32345 files, 7448 links). Also measured: cargo metadata does NOT execute build.rs or proc macros (marker-file probe, both absent, exit 0) and reports custom-build/proc-macro target kinds plus links and source, so the pre-compile rejection matrix is decidable in the graph phase; --locked prevents any Cargo.lock write into the frozen snapshot; a package .cargo/config.toml rustc-wrapper DID run a package-selected executable and an ancestor .cargo/config.toml is also discovered, while RUSTC_WRAPPER= in the manager environment neutralised both and a config [env] force=true could not override it; rust-toolchain.toml carrying both path and nightly is fully inert against a directly resolved cargo. rust-version has three host-independent acceptance layers (TOML type, RustVersion grammar, edition floor) plus a separate host gate, each with distinct measured diagnostics. Writing decision 0009 + reference + boundary probe next.\nHANDOFF 2026-07-29: decision 0009 + implementation-ready reference + executable boundary probe, all attached. Two decisive host measurements. (1) Process closure: with SDKROOT and -Clinker=<root>/lib/rustlib/<target>/bin/rust-lld -Clinker-flavor=ld64.lld pinned, both the graph and the compile phase produced ZERO PATH resolutions against 20 logging shims and yielded a running Mach-O arm64 binary depending only on libSystem; the unpinned control resolved xcrun and cc. Closure is cargo->rustc->rust-lld inside the fingerprinted Rust root, with the macOS SDK as a data-only second root, so no sixth toolchain identifier is coined and toolchain_identities stays at one element. (2) cargo metadata executes no build.rs and no proc macro (marker probe, both absent, exit 0) while reporting custom-build/proc-macro/links/source, which is what makes the decision 0008 section 7 pre-compile matrix computable. Also measured: --locked prevents a Cargo.lock write into the frozen snapshot; a package and an ancestor .cargo/config.toml both execute a package-named rustc wrapper, neutralised by an empty RUSTC_WRAPPER but rejected outright anyway; rust-toolchain.toml is inert against direct resolution. One correction to decision 0007: Cargo.toml rust-version moves from compared to classified because it has three measured host-independent acceptance layers (TOML type, grammar, edition floor) plus an excluded host gate, with F empty so P1/P2 collapse to C = Upstream. Probe green exit 0: 19/19 cases, 24 closure checks 0 verdicts, 6/6 controls failing as required, 8/8 structural checks. platforms holds only (macos, arm64); macOS amd64, Windows and Linux are qualification obligations with a stated acceptance test, never claims. Two residual exposures stated not closed: compile-time file inclusion (needs a seventh deferred guarantee in STORY-260728-327soo) and FFI against base-installation libraries. Gates: probe gofmt/vet/build/test 0, probe runs 0, curator build/vet/test/gofmt 0; make check 2 and spec validate.py 1 are expected-red and attributed to other tasks trees, with a clean-tree validate baseline at 0 and a scoped link check over the two authored documents at 0. golangci-lint NOT RUN, not installed on this host. Decision number 0009 reserved; renumbers if Swift or Kotlin lands it first.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-52b118, pid=90707, exit=0)\nREVIEW CYCLE 1 DIRECTIVE: Independently review the Rust pair; do not edit artifacts. Treat accepted decisions 0007/0008 as authoritative and reject silent contract drift. Specifically adjudicate the proposed rust