n by a shipped schema; the claim-v4 slot stays unminted, so the claim gate is proved against shipped claim v3 plus a synthetic newer sibling. Nothing staged, committed, published, pinned or claimed; no platform or native validation claim. Artifacts: TASK-260728-2spy93_rework-02.md (new) and the updated TASK-260728-2spy93_decision-0008-additional-language-driver-boundary.md.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-cf840f, pid=56648, exit=0)\nREVIEW CYCLE 3 directive 2026-07-28: independently verify both cycle-2 blockers are closed in the final rework. For buildCommandV8, repositoryBuildCommandV2 and skillBuildTargetV2, prove toolchain is exactly the sole $ref to #/$defs/toolchainRequirementV1 with no siblings, and that the referenced closed definition is exactly id+version/additionalProperties=false; challenge dangling refs, wrong refs, string/open/path-bearing objects, and a reserved shape lacking driver. For claim-v4, verify assertion membership equals exactly the admitted driver set at minting, every driver maps to its fixed execution policy, retired identifiers are structurally impossible, all-six acceptance yields eight while Kotlin retirement does not, and frozen older claims may remain subsets without widening current admission. Re-run all 71 tests, plant-and-revert adversarial probes, deterministic regeneration twice and unchanged rc.5 release/digest gates. No edits, staging, commit, publication, pin or platform claim; attach explicit verdict and route status.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-0a342c, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-0a342c)\nReview cycle