de\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-fae629, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-fae629)\nRework 03 complete and ready for review. Both cycle-3 blockers closed in the existing task worktree; still exactly three files different from the accepted TASK-260728-2kp3tv base (decision 0008 now 1009 lines, tools/validate.py, tools/test_validate.py). (1) The object type is now part of the closure itself: check_closed_member_set requires "type": "object" exactly, so toolchainRequirementV1 declared as a string, with no type, or as an [object,string] union all reject, and every deployed/reserved/manager-authored closed definition is held to the same rule. All nine shipped closed definitions already declared type object, so no shipped shape moved. (2) Claim admission is closed at the container: conformance_claim_schemas() picks the newest schema BEFORE any filtering and that schema MUST declare build_drivers, so a newer claim can no longer drop the member and hand currency back to a frozen predecessor; new check_claim_driver_container closes the array to keywords that cannot reach an element, so prefixItems, contains, unevaluatedItems, additionalItems and any applicator added later reject as unlisted rather than being interpreted, items must be exactly {oneOf: [...]}, and each assertion is closed by keyword set and must declare type object. Decision text made precise, not reopened: section 4 placement, section 8 assertion-list closure, section 11 items 6/8/9, Security impact. Mutant probe (.temp/TASK-260728-2spy93/mutant-probe.py) restores both cycle-2 checker bodies and proves all three reviewer mutants were ACCEPTED before and are REJECTED after, plus that the prefixItems escape is real under the compiled Draft 2020-12 validator (shipped claim rejects the reserved driver with 1 error, prefixItems variant accepts it with 0). Gates green standalone: validate.py 0 (42 schemas / 422 files), unittest 0 (76 tests, was 71), go test 0, go vet 0, gofmt 0, compileall 0, git diff --check 0, mutant probe 0. Clean-checkout probe at commit 86ec275: make validate 0, make regenerate-check 0 twice, make release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.5 0. rc.5 preserved byte-identical: manifest 9ba9b8ec..., release/1.0.0-rc.5.json b32ee9d3..., both equal to the accepted base. Six plant-and-revert probes, every planted file restored byte-identical: string toolchainRequirementV1 rejected by the boundary gate, the same definition minted as an object accepted (so the check is not vacuously rejecting), and the boundary gate isolated on a planted open prefixItems assertion accepted under the cycle-2 checker and rejected under the shipped one. Honest limitation: on-disk plants against the shipped claim v3 are caught by earlier layers (reserved-name absence scan, frozen schema-case corpus), so the container closure is what owns a newly minted claim version whose identifiers and negative cases are authored by the same change - reachable only by unit test and in-memory probe until TASK-260728-251p01 mints claim v4; the reserved shapes and toolchainRequirementV1 still do not exist on disk. Nothing staged, committed, published, pinned or claimed; no platform or native validation claim. Artifact: TASK-260728-2spy93_rework-03.md (new) plus the updated decision attachment, sha256 36f98739...\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-fae629, pid=78805, exit=0)\nREVIEW CYCLE 4 directive 2026-07-28: independently reproduce closure of every cycle-3 mutant against the final task worktree. Verify toolchainRequirementV1 requires type:object exactly and rejects string, omitted type, and object|string unions while retaining exact id+version closure. Verify newest claim schema is selected before inspection and must declare build_drivers; its container permits no parallel element path, including prefixItems, contains, unevaluatedItems, additionalItems or future unlisted applicators; items is exactly oneOf and each assertion is a closed object. Reproduce the three exact mutants from TASK-260728-2spy93_review-verdict-cycle-3.md, challenge equivalent schema routes, run all 76 tests, Draft 2020-12 probe, Go/format/diff gates, deterministic regeneration twice, and unchanged rc.5 release/digests. Confirm exactly the three owned files differ and frozen schemas 1-7/Go identities remain untouched. No edits/staging/commit/publication/pin/platform claim; attach explicit ACCEPTED or CHANGES REQUESTED verdict and route status.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-d42d75, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-d42d75)\nReview cycle 4 logbook 2026-07-28 — CHANGES REQUESTED. All requested gates are green and every cycle-3 mutant is closed, but the artifact boundary gate still false-accepts buildArtifactV1 widened to an object|string union and false-accepts removal of required path/digest/size members. Exact evidence and narrow re-review gate: TASK-260728-2spy93_review-verdict-cycle-4.md. Routed to to-dev for ordinary implementation rework. Reviewer changed no project file, staging, commit, publication, pin, or platform claim.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-d42d75, pid=89689, exit=0)\nREWORK CYCLE 4 directive 2026-07-28: close only the single blocker in TASK-260728-2spy93_review-verdict-cycle-4.md, preserving every accepted cycle-1 th