   657	### 12. Platform matrix
   658	
   659	| Platform | Status |
   660	|---|---|
   661	| macOS arm64 | the complete pipeline is measured on one host; it enters a claim only through `TASK-260728-2bu2q6` with immutable native evidence for that exact tuple |
   662	| macOS amd64 | qualification obligation; the standard library ships in the same root, and the acceptance test is a probe run on an x86_64 macOS host |
   663	| Windows | implementation contract only, stated below; **no** platform claim, because no reachable Windows host had a Rust toolchain |
   664	| Linux | excluded until `TASK-260728-1skseh`, then qualified by the same acceptance test |
   665	
   666	**Windows implementation contract.** The Windows obligation is to reproduce
   667	section 2's property — a process closure with no `PATH`-resolved executable —
   668	and it has two candidate paths, neither of which this decision claims:
   669	
   670	1. `x86_64-pc-windows-msvc` with `-C linker=<root>/lib/rustlib/<target>/bin/rust-lld`
   671	   and `-C linker-flavor=lld-link`, with the MSVC and Windows SDK import
   672	   libraries bound as one or more data-only `platform-sdk` link-support roots.
   673	   `lld-link` is present in the same `gcc-ld` directory as the macOS flavours on
   674	   the measured root, which makes this the path to test first.
   675	2. `x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` with the target's bundled self-contained linking
   676	   artifacts, which if sufficient would need no link-support root at all.
   677	
   678	The acceptance test for either is exactly the one run on macOS: the twenty-shim
   679	poisoned-`PATH` run must produce zero entries for both the graph and the compile
   680	phase, with a control run that produces entries when the pins are removed, and
   681	the produced executable must depend only on base-installation libraries. Until
   682	that evidence exists, `platforms` excludes Windows and both drivers fail
   683	`build_toolchain_platform_unsupported` there. An implementation MUST NOT ship a
   684	Windows path that resolves `link.exe`, `cl.exe`, `gcc`, `ld`, `vswhere` or a
   685	Visual Studio activation script from `PATH`, the registry, or an environment
   686	variable, and MUST NOT answer the gap with a host-resolved tool or a downgraded
   687	control.
   688	
   689	**Linux qualification rules.** Linux enters `platforms` only when, on the
   690	qualifying host: `rustc --print host-tuple` reports a tuple whose standard
   691	library is present in the fingerprinted root by the section 3 stat; the
   692	poisoned-`PATH` run is clean for both phases with a firing control; the produced
   693	ELF executable's dynamic dependencies are all base-installation libraries of the
   694	declared distribution baseline; and the `platform-sdk` role is either absent or
   695	resolved from a declaration channel. `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu` will require a
   696	`platform-sdk` link-support root holding the C runtime startup objects and
   697	`libc` stubs, and `x86_64-unknown-linux-musl` may not, which is the qualification
   698	question rather than a claim.
