   146	## 2. `curator-rust-toolchain-v1`
   147	
   148	### 2.1 Resolution
   149	
   150	The Rust distribution root and every `link_support_roles` root are resolved
   151	through exactly the two declaration channels of decision 0007 section 3 —
   152	`operator_config` then `bundled` — and through nothing else. `PATH`, the
   153	inherited environment (including `RUSTUP_HOME`, `CARGO_HOME`, `RUSTC`,
   154	`RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN`, `DEVELOPER_DIR`, `SDKROOT`, `TOOLCHAINS`), a runtime root,
   155	project `.agents/bin`, any shim, a manifest or descriptor value, `xcrun`,
   156	`xcode-select` and any version-manager wrapper (`rustup`, `asdf`, `mise`) are
   157	forbidden origins with the diagnostics decision 0007 section 5 fixes. An
   158	operator MAY configure the concrete root that `rustup` produced; the manager
   159	resolves that root directly and never through the shim.
   160	
   161	Inside the resolved Rust distribution root the manager requires three regular
   162	executables, and starts no other program below the worker:
   163	
   164	| Relpath | Role |
   165	|---|---|
   166	| `bin/cargo` | trusted launcher, the `primary_relpath` |
   167	| `bin/rustc` | compiler |
   168	| `lib/rustlib/<native-tuple>/bin/rust-lld` | linker |
   169	
   170	Each MUST be a regular executable inside the tree being fingerprinted, never a
   171	wrapper and never outside it. A missing or non-regular member is
   172	`build_toolchain_untrusted` with `substep` = `shape`.
   173	
   174	### 2.2 Identity
   175	
   176	`curator-rust-toolchain-v1` produces exactly:
   177	
   178	```json
   179	{
   180	  "algorithm": "curator-rust-toolchain-v1",
   181	  "rust_version": "release: 1.91.0",
   182	  "cargo_version": "cargo 1.91.0 (ea2d97820 2025-10-10)",
   183	  "launcher_relpath": "bin/cargo",
   184	  "rustc_relpath": "bin/rustc",
   185	  "linker_relpath": "lib/rustlib/aarch64-apple-darwin/bin/rust-lld",
   186	  "roots": [
   187	    {"role": "rust-distribution", "tree_sha256": "sha256:<hex>"},
   188	    {"role": "platform-sdk",      "tree_sha256": "sha256:<hex>"}
   189	  ],
   190	  "closure_sha256": "sha256:<hex>"
   191	}
   192	```
   193	
   194	`roles` is the closed token set `{rust-distribution, platform-sdk}`. No root
   195	path appears anywhere in the identity: toolchain location is not portable
   196	identity. The `roots` array is ordered `rust-distribution` first, then each
   197	`link_support_roles` entry in its registry order.
   198	
   199	Per-root `tree_sha256` uses the walk, ordering, record framing, link rules and
   200	`kind` alphabet of `curator-go-toolchain-v1` — walk without following links, the
   201	root itself is not a record, relative components must be valid Unicode scalar
   202	values, `/`-joined paths encoded as UTF-8 without case folding or normalization,
   203	duplicate encoded paths and special files rejected, symlinks relative and
   204	non-dangling and resolving within the root with independent tree records for
   205	their referents, hard links as independent regular-file records, path bytes
   206	sorted in unsigned bytewise order — with SHA-256 initialized by the exact ASCII
   207	`curator-rust-toolchain-v1/<role>` followed by `0x00` and each entry appended as:
   208	
   209	```text
   210	kind || uint64be(path_byte_length) || path_utf8 ||
   211	uint64be(payload_byte_length) || payload
   212	```
   213	
   214	The `rust-distribution` root appends two final records with empty paths: `V`
   215	carrying the normalized `rustc -vV` stdout and `C` carrying the normalized
   216	`cargo --version` stdout, each normalized by requiring at most 4096 bytes and
   217	exactly one terminal LF optionally preceded by CR, removing that terminator, and
   218	rejecting any other CR, LF, NUL, empty or invalid UTF-8 content. A
   219	`platform-sdk` root appends no version record.
   220	
   221	`closure_sha256` initializes SHA-256 with the exact ASCII
   222	`curator-rust-toolchain-v1/closure` followed by `0x00` and appends, for each
   223	element of `roots` in order:
   224	
   225	```text
   226	ASCII("R") || uint64be(role_byte_length) || role_ascii ||
   227	uint64be(32) || raw_tree_digest_bytes
   228	```
   229	
   230	so a one-root closure and a two-root closure can never collide even if their
   231	tree digests coincide. Prefix every emitted digest with `sha256:`.
   232	
   233	Permissions, ownership, timestamps, ACLs and extended attributes are not hash
   234	inputs, but the three executables of section 2.1 MUST be regular and executable
   235	at use time. Every root MUST remain unchanged through the last child exit, and
   236	every identity MUST be re-verified after the last child exits and before
   237	publication; a change rejects the operation before publication.
   238	
   239	**Measured cost**, same host: the Rust distribution root is 657 MB across 167
   240	regular files and hashes in 1.73 s wall clock; the macOS SDK root is 261 MB
   241	across 32,345 regular files and 7,448 symlinks and hashes in 9.01 s. The cost is
   242	per operation and per root and MUST NOT be memoised across operations.
