   272	## 4. The two argument vectors
   273	
   274	The working directory is the canonical `source_dir` for both. Neither the parent
   275	nor the worker MAY alter, extend, reorder or repeat them.
   276	
   277	```text
   278	cargo metadata --format-version 1 --locked --offline --color never --quiet
   279	cargo build --locked --offline --color never --quiet --release --target <native-tuple> --bin <bin-target-name>
   280	```
   281	
   282	`<native-tuple>` is the Stage A resolved host tuple. `<bin-target-name>` is the
   283	single `bin` target name from the graph phase, validated against
   284	`^[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,63}$` **before** it is placed in an argument
   285	vector; a name outside that grammar is `build_rust_bin_target_invalid` and no
   286	compile phase starts.
   287	
   288	`--locked` is load-bearing. **Measured**: without it, `cargo metadata` writes
   289	`Cargo.lock` into the source tree — a write to the frozen snapshot. With it and
   290	no lock file present, `cargo metadata` exits **101** with
   291	`error: the lock file <path> needs to be updated but --locked was passed to
   292	prevent this` and writes nothing.
   293	
   294	The produced file is:
   295	
   296	```text
   297	<CARGO_TARGET_DIR>/<native-tuple>/release/<bin-target-name>          (Unix)
   298	<CARGO_TARGET_DIR>\<native-tuple>\release\<bin-target-name>.exe      (Windows)
   299	```
   300	
   301	`CARGO_TARGET_DIR` is an operation-private manager staging root. The manager
   302	hashes the file there, sets manager-defined executable permissions, publishes it
   303	as `bin/<command>` or `bin/<command>.exe` derived solely from the consuming
   304	manifest command key, and MUST NOT execute it for validation, version discovery,
   305	smoke testing, post-processing, receipt generation, rollback or any other
   306	reason. Every other file in the target directory is a compiler by-product,
   307	stays in staging, is discarded with it, and never enters cache identity, the
   308	receipt, the marker, the shim relationship or publication.
   309	
   310	## 5. Operation-private environment
   311	
   312	The environment starts empty except for indispensable operating-system process
   313	variables, and is identical for the probe vectors, the graph phase and the
   314	compile phase.
   315	
   316	| Variable | Value |
   317	|---|---|
   318	| `PATH` | a manager-owned empty directory |
   319	| `HOME`, `TMPDIR`, `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, `XDG_CACHE_HOME` | operation-private roots |
   320	| `APPDATA`, `LOCALAPPDATA`, `USERPROFILE`, `TEMP`, `TMP` | operation-private roots, Windows only |
   321	| `LC_ALL`, `LANG` | `C` |
   322	| `CARGO_HOME` | operation-private root holding only the manager-written config of section 5.1 |
   323	| `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` | operation-private staging root |
   324	| `RUSTC` | absolute `<root>/bin/rustc` |
   325	| `RUSTDOC` | absolute `<root>/bin/rustdoc` |
   326	| `RUSTC_WRAPPER`, `RUSTC_WORKSPACE_WRAPPER` | set and empty |
   327	| `CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS` | exactly `-Clinker=<root>/lib/rustlib/<native-tuple>/bin/rust-lld` `0x1F` `-Clinker-flavor=<flavor>` |
   328	| `CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTDOCFLAGS` | set and empty |
   329	| `CARGO_INCREMENTAL` | `0` |
   330	| `CARGO_NET_OFFLINE` | `true` |
   331	| `CARGO_NET_RETRY` | `0` |
   332	| `CARGO_NET_GIT_FETCH_WITH_CLI` | `false` |
   333	| `CARGO_TERM_COLOR` | `never` |
   334	| `SDKROOT` | the resolved `platform-sdk` root, macOS only |
   335	
   336	`<flavor>` is `ld64.lld` on macOS. Windows and Linux flavours are qualification
   337	obligations, section 12.
   338	
   339	Every other Rust, Cargo, `rustup`, compiler, linker, SDK and executable-search
   340	variable MUST be absent, and none may be inherited. In particular
   341	`RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP` MUST be absent, because it makes a release toolchain accept
   342	`-Z` flags; and `RUSTFLAGS`, `RUSTDOCFLAGS`, `CARGO_BUILD_*` other than the
   343	target directory, `CARGO_TARGET_*_LINKER`, `CARGO_TARGET_*_RUSTFLAGS`,
   344	`CARGO_REGISTRIES_*`, `CARGO_REGISTRY_*`, `CARGO_HTTP_*`, `CARGO_UNSTABLE_*`,
   345	`RUSTUP_*`, `RUSTC_LOG`, `DEVELOPER_DIR`, `MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET`,
   346	`LD_LIBRARY_PATH`, `DYLD_*`, `LIBRARY_PATH`, `CPATH`, `CC`, `CXX` and `AR` MUST
   347	be absent.
   348	
   349	Three of these are answers to measured behaviour rather than hygiene:
   350	
   351	- **`RUSTC` absolute.** Cargo otherwise resolves `rustc` by name from `PATH`;
   352	  under a minimal `PATH` `TASK-260729-rhjxtx` measured
   353	  `could not execute process 'rustc -vV' (never executed)`, and under a
   354	  populated one the second node of the process graph would be chosen by `PATH`
   355	  order.
   356	- **`SDKROOT` set.** **Measured**: without it, `rustc` runs
   357	  `xcrun --sdk macosx --show-sdk-path` resolved from `PATH`; with it, no `xcrun`
   358	  lookup occurs.
   359	- **`RUSTC_WRAPPER` and `RUSTC_WORKSPACE_WRAPPER` set and empty.** **Measured**:
   360	  a package `.cargo/config.toml` carrying `[build] rustc-wrapper` executed the
   361	  named script three times during `cargo build`; setting `RUSTC_WRAPPER` to the
   362	  empty string in the manager environment neutralised it, and a config
   363	  `[env] RUSTC_WRAPPER = { value = "...", force = true }` did not override the
   364	  neutralisation.
   365	
   366	Environment neutralisation is a second layer, never the answer. `[source]`,
   367	`[registries]`, `[patch]` and `[http]` config tables have no environment
   368	counterpart and a package config file outranks the manager's own `$CARGO_HOME`
   369	config, so L5 rejects the file outright.
   370	
   371	**Measured**: a `.cargo/config.toml` in an *ancestor* directory above the build
   372	root is discovered and applied. The manager MUST therefore guarantee that no
   373	`.cargo` directory exists in any ancestor of the compile working directory, up
   374	to the filesystem root. That is a manager staging obligation; when it cannot be
   375	met the operation fails `build_execution_control_unavailable` before the worker
   376	starts.
   377	
   378	### 5.1 The manager-written `$CARGO_HOME/config.toml`
   379	
   380	Written by the manager before the graph phase, with exactly these four tables
   381	and nothing else:
   382	
   383	```toml
   384	[source.crates-io]
   385	replace-with = "curator-vendor"
   386	
   387	[source.curator-vendor]
   388	directory = "<absolute path of <build_root>/vendor>"
   389	
   390	[net]
   391	offline = true
   392	
   393	[term]
   394	quiet = true
   395	color = "never"
   396	```
   397	
   398	The only package-derived component is the driver-fixed relative path `vendor`
   399	under the build root. No package or descriptor byte reaches this file, and the
   400	manager MUST NOT write any other key into it.
   401	
   402	## 6. Pre-compile rejection matrix
   403	
   404	Computed from the validated snapshot and the graph phase, before the compile
   405	phase. Total by construction: every row has one verdict, and the list of rows is
   406	closed. Rows are evaluated in the order given; the first failure is the reported
   407	diagnostic.
   408	
   409	### 6.1 Graph-phase properties
   410	
   411	**Measured**: `cargo metadata --format-version 1 --offline` over a build root
   412	whose path dependency declares `build = "build.rs"` with a `build.rs` that
   413	writes a marker file, and whose second path dependency declares
   414	`[lib] proc-macro = true` with a macro that writes a second marker file,
   415	produced **neither** marker and exited 0. The same run reported
   416	`kind: ["custom-build"]` for the build-script target, `kind: ["proc-macro"]` and
   417	`crate_types: ["proc-macro"]` for the macro crate, `links: "probelib"` for the
   418	package declaring a native library, and a `source` value per package.
   419	
   420	The graph command is run **without** `--filter-platform`, so `packages[]` is the
   421	union over every platform and every feature rather than this host's resolution.
   422	The matrix is therefore host-independent, and it over-approximates: a dependency
   423	that would only be built on another platform, or only under a feature this build
   424	does not enable, still rejects the command. That is the accepted trade.
   425	
   426	### 6.2 Rows decided by the graph phase
   427	
   428	Let `R` be the build root and `V` be `<R>/vendor`.
   429	
   430	| # | Rejected when | Diagnostic |
   431	|---|---|---|
   432	| G1 | `workspace_members` has other than exactly one element, or that element is not the `R` package, or `resolve.root` is null or differs | `build_rust_workspace_forbidden` |
   433	| G2 | any package has a target whose `kind` contains `custom-build` | `build_rust_build_script_forbidden` |
   434	| G3 | any package has a target whose `kind` or `crate_types` contains `proc-macro` | `build_rust_proc_macro_forbidden` |
   435	| G4 | any package has a non-null `links` | `build_rust_native_link_declaration_forbidden` |
   436	| G5 | any package `source` is neither null nor exactly `registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index` | `build_rust_dependency_source_forbidden` |
   437	| G6 | a package with null `source` has a `manifest_path` outside `R`, or any target `src_path` outside `R` | `build_rust_input_outside_build_root` |
   438	| G7 | a package with the crates.io `source` has a `manifest_path` outside `V` | `build_rust_input_outside_build_root` |
   439	| G8 | any target has a `crate_types` member outside `{bin, lib, rlib}` | `build_rust_crate_type_forbidden` |
   440	| G9 | the `R` package has other than exactly one target whose `kind` is exactly `["bin"]` | `build_rust_bin_target_ambiguous` |
   441	| G10 | that target's `name` is outside `^[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,63}$` | `build_rust_bin_target_invalid` |
   442	
   443	G2, G3, G4, G5 and G8 are the `build_package_code_execution_forbidden` semantic
   444	class; the rest are driver-specific structural rejections. G5 covers git
   445	dependencies, alternate registries, `local-registry` and `sparse` sources and any
   446	future source kind, because it is an exact-match allowlist of two values rather
   447	than a deny-list. **Measured**: a git dependency under `--offline` fails inside
   448	the graph phase with `error: failed to get 'anyhow' as a dependency of package
   449	'gd v0.1.0 (...)'` / `Caused by: failed to load source for dependency 'anyhow'`,
   450	before any compile phase, so G5 has a fail-closed backstop in cargo itself.
   451	
   452	### 6.3 Rows decided by snapshot bytes
   453	
   454	L5 and L7 of section 3, plus the closed native-input extension list of L6, case
   455	folded for comparison:
   456	
   457	```text
   458	.o .obj .a .lib .so .dylib .dll .tbd .rlib .rmeta .bc .ll .pdb .exp .res
   459	.s .S .asm .c .cc .cpp .cxx .h .hh .hpp .m .mm .def .rc
   460	```
   461	
   462	and any path component ending in `.framework` or `.dSYM`. A match is
   463	`build_rust_native_input_forbidden`. This is defence in depth over an already
   464	closed path — without build scripts there is no admitted way to compile or link
   465	such a file — and it is the direct analogue of `go-v1`'s `SysoFiles`, `CFiles`
   466	and `SFiles` rejection.
   467	
   468	### 6.4 Rows decided by the fixed environment and argument vectors
   469	
   470	| Surface | Closed by |
   471	|---|---|
   472	| network, registry index, git fetch, crate download | `--offline`, `--locked`, `CARGO_NET_OFFLINE`, the manager-written config, and an empty `PATH` |
   473	| package-selected linker, linker flavour, link argument, library search path | `CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS` fixed by the manager, no package config file, no build script |
   474	| package-selected `rustc`, `rustdoc`, wrapper | absolute `RUSTC` and `RUSTDOC`, empty `RUSTC_WRAPPER` and `RUSTC_WORKSPACE_WRAPPER` |
   475	| `-Z` flags, unstable manifest keys, nightly features | release-channel toolchain, `RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP` absent, `cargo-features` rejected by L7 |
   476	| cross-compilation | `--target` fixed to the resolved native tuple |
   477	| incremental state | `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0` |
   478	| package-selected toolchain path, root, channel, mirror, installer, version manager | decision 0007 resolution; `rust-toolchain*` classified rather than honoured, section 7 |
   479	
   480	### 6.5 Admitted surfaces
   481	
   482	Cargo **features** are admitted: they select which package source compiles,
   483	which is the same class of choice as a Go build constraint, and the build always
   484	uses the root package's default feature resolution because the command object
   485	cannot express one.
   486	
   487	`[profile]` tables are admitted: on a release toolchain per-profile `rustflags`
   488	are gated behind `-Z profile-rustflags`, and both `-Z` flags and the
   489	`cargo-features` opt-in that would unlock them are rejected, so a profile selects
   490	codegen tuning and cannot inject a flag or start a process. Link-time
   491	optimisation stays inside `rustc` and its bundled LLVM.
   492	
   493	Two further surfaces are admitted with bounds and are stated as residual
   494	exposures rather than closed; see section 11.
   495	
   496	## 7. Stage B — metadata dispositions
   497	
   498	Decision 0007's disposition framework, precedence rule, file-shape gate and
   499	channel classification are fixed there and are not reopened. Files are evaluated
   500	in Unicode-scalar lexical order of relative source path, so `Cargo.toml`
   501	precedes `rust-toolchain` precedes `rust-toolchain.toml`; within each file
   502	`forbidden` classes precede `compared` classes.
   503	
   504	| Source | Field | Disposition |
   505	|---|---|---|
   506	| `Cargo.toml` | `package.rust-version` | `classified`, section 7.2 |
   507	| `Cargo.toml` | `workspace.package.rust-version` | unreachable: a workspace is rejected by G1 |
   508	| `rust-toolchain.toml` | `toolchain.path` | `forbidden` |
   509	| `rust-toolchain.toml` | `toolchain.channel` | `compared`, section 7.3 |
   510	| `rust-toolchain.toml` | `toolchain.components`, `toolchain.targets`, `toolchain.profile` | `ignored` |
   511	| `rust-toolchain` | the bare channel string | `compared`, section 7.3 |
   512	
   513	**Measured**: a build root carrying a `rust-toolchain.toml` with *both*
   514	`path = "/nonexistent"` and `channel = "nightly"` built successfully through a
   515	directly resolved `cargo`, with zero `PATH` resolutions. The same file redirects
   516	the `rustup` shim — `TASK-260729-rhjxtx` measured `error: invalid toolchain: the
   517	path '/nonexistent/trusted/root' has no bin/ directory` for `path`, and
   518	`info: syncing channel updates for 'nightly-aarch64-apple-darwin'` followed by a
   519	download attempt for `channel = "nightly"`. The file is a live selector through
   520	the shim and completely inert against direct resolution, which is exactly what
   521	admits `channel` as `compared` and keeps `path` `forbidden`.
   522	
   523	### 7.1 File-shape gate
   524	
   525	For each `metadata_sources` file present in the validated tree, the gate covers
   526	file **syntax** only: a file the ecosystem's own grammar rejects, including a
   527	key the ecosystem permits at most once appearing more than once, is
   528	`build_toolchain_metadata_mismatch` with `assertion` = `unclassifiable` and a
   529	`source_ref` naming the file or the field path. It asserts nothing about the
   530	semantics of fields the entry does not read.

