   492	| Driver | Execution policy |
   493	|---|---|
   494	| `go-v1`, `go-repository-v1` | `manager-worker-v1` |
   495	| the six reserved identifiers | `manager-worker-v2` |
   496	
   497	`manager-worker-v2` carries the identical portable containment contract. The
   498	mandatory portable control set of `protocol/core.md` section 4.2.1, the
   499	exhaustive `rc5-native-control-inventory-v1` inventory, the single
   500	`build_execution_control_unavailable` failure boundary, the exclusion of host
   501	capability evidence from cache identity, and the six deferred hardened
   502	guarantees are the same under both identities, byte for byte and control for
   503	control. No control is added, removed, re-scoped, or weakened. The inventory
   504	keeps its `rc5-` name because its membership is unchanged and inventory
   505	membership never enters a build input, an artifact, or a hashed identity.
   506	
   507	Exactly two things differ, and they are exactly the two things that could not be
   508	said generically about v1 without reinterpreting it.
   509	
   510	First, the two lower graph nodes are bound per driver rather than to Go:
   511	
   512	```text
   513	manager parent
   514	  -> identity-verified manager-owned worker
   515	       -> the driver's fingerprinted trusted launcher
   516	            -> fingerprinted regular executables inside that driver's
   517	               fingerprinted trusted toolchain closure
   518	```
