   700	## 8. Identity, cache, receipt, marker, claim
   701	
   702	The canonical build input binds, in addition to the members decision 0008
   703	section 8 requires of every new driver:
   704	
   705	- the complete `curator-rust-toolchain-v1` identity of section 2, including both
   706	  per-root digests and `closure_sha256`, as the single element of
   707	  `toolchain_identities`;
   708	- the resolved native tuple;
   709	- the validated `bin` target name; and
   710	- this closed policy object, whose `execution_policy` is the `const`
   711	  `manager-worker-v2`:
   712	
   713	```json
   714	{
   715	  "dependency_mode": "vendor-directory",
   716	  "network": "none",
   717	  "workspace": false,
   718	  "build_scripts": false,
   719	  "proc_macros": false,
   720	  "plugins": false,
   721	  "features": "manifest-default",
   722	  "target_mode": "native",
   723	  "profile": "release",
   724	  "linker": "toolchain-rust-lld",
   725	  "link_mode": "internal",
   726	  "native_inputs": false,
   727	  "package_config": "rejected",
   728	  "compiler_directives": "reject-nonstandard-native-inputs-v1",
   729	  "incremental": false,
   730	  "execution_policy": "manager-worker-v2"
   731	}
   732	```
   733	
   734	`network: "none"` denotes the fixed offline Cargo configuration, `--offline`,
   735	`--locked`, the manager-written `$CARGO_HOME` config and the empty `PATH`. It is
   736	not a claim of kernel-enforced network denial; that guarantee is
   737	`total-network-denial`, deferred to `STORY-260728-327soo`.
   738	
   739	The logical cache key is the SHA-256 of `CCJ-1` over the complete input, exactly
   740	as for the Go drivers. Receipt schema 3 carries the local mode and schema 4 the
   741	external mode, each a strict `oneOf` discriminated by the `driver` `const`.
   742	Marker schema 4 records `driver`, `receipt_schema_version` and
   743	`execution_policy` per build entry; a reader rejects a `rust-v1` entry claiming
   744	`manager-worker-v1` rather than inferring the policy from the driver name.
   745	Conformance claim schema 4 asserts each identifier with `execution_policy`
   746	selected by the assertion's own `driver` `const`.
   747	
   748	The effective toolchain requirement and the `compatibility` set are gates, not
   749	build inputs.
   750	
   751	`rust-repository-v1`'s input additionally carries the members decision 0008
   752	section 5 and `protocol/core.md` section 9.2 already fix for an external
   753	command — repository identifier, declared and effective source state,
   754	substitution, external `curator-build-source-v1`, descriptor path and selected
   755	target — plus `"source_kind":"locked-external-git-v1"`.
