   791	## 10. Artifact
   792	
   793	Exactly one bounded regular file, class `native-executable-v1`.
   794	
   795	**Measured** on this host: the pipeline produces a `Mach-O 64-bit executable
   796	arm64` whose only dynamic dependency reported by `otool -L` is
   797	`/usr/lib/libSystem.B.dylib`, a base-installation library, and whose code
   798	signature is `adhoc, linker-signed`. That signature is applied by `rust-lld` as
   799	part of linking: it is produced by the driver's fixed argument vector, selects no
   800	signing identity, credential, entitlement or notarization, and reaches no
   801	network. It is compiler output, not a manager signing step. The driver performs
   802	no manager post-build signing, timestamping or notarization, and a platform
   803	policy requiring a locally signed binary must wait for the separately versioned
   804	and reviewed signer profile.
   805	
   806	The driver does not require bit-reproducible artifacts.
   807	
   808	## 11. Residual exposures
   809	
   810	Two surfaces are admitted with bounds rather than rejected. Both are stated so
   811	that no reader, receipt, marker or claim can imply otherwise.
   812	
   813	**Compile-time file inclusion.** `include!`, `include_str!` and `include_bytes!`
   814	resolve a path relative to the including file and can name a path outside the
   815	build root. They are reads, not code execution, so decision 0008 section 7 does
   816	not require their rejection; the portable policy does not contain the compiler's
   817	filesystem access, and none of the six deferred hardened guarantees covers
   818	compile-time reads. No sound deterministic pre-compile rejection exists: the
   819	macro name is a token rather than a byte pattern, so `include ! ( "x" )` and
   820	`cfg_attr` forms defeat a byte scan, while a scan for the substring `include`
   821	rejects ordinary comments and identifiers. Recorded as a new input to
   822	`STORY-260728-327soo`.
   823	
   824	**Foreign function declarations against base-installation libraries.** Package
   825	source may declare `extern` blocks and `#[link]` attributes. The package cannot
   826	supply a library to link — native files are rejected by L6, `links` by G4, build
   827	scripts by G2, and no admitted path adds a library search path — so `#[link]`
   828	can only name a library the pinned link environment already resolves, which is a
   829	base-installation library. Decision 0008 section 3 already requires the artifact
   830	to depend on exactly those. This is not a claim that the produced program is
   831	safe; it remains untrusted package output the manager never executes.
   832	
