   316	observable: with `go build ./...` as the `toolchain`-position command, the module
   317	loader runs after selection and exits non-zero on `toolchain default` and
   318	`toolchain go1` with `updates to go.mod needed`, which is not a statement about
   319	the name — and a fall-through branch that named acceptance scored both as
   320	upstream acceptance on both probed toolchains. Two rules follow. The command is
   321	narrowed to the one whose only failure surface is the layer under test, which for
   322	the `toolchain` position is `go version`; and an outcome outside the recognised
   323	set is *unknown*, fails the probe, and yields no verdict for the agreement check
   324	to consume. Closure is what makes a green probe evidence rather than an absence
   325	of surprises.
   326	
   327	**A closed set is a set of outcomes, not of leads.** The first attempt at closure
   328	still recognised *families*: a prefix with an unconstrained tail, a substring
   329	found anywhere in the output. A family answers for every message upstream might
   330	later render behind that lead, and none of them has been measured. Reading both
   331	probed toolchains' `toolchain.Select` settles the case concretely: its
   332	colon-bearing `invalid GOTOOLCHAIN %q` calls quote the *environment* setting
   333	while interpreting it, before `go.mod` is read at all, so under the probe's fixed
   334	`GOTOOLCHAIN=local+path` they quote `local+path` and can never name the value
   335	under test. A branch admitting `invalid GOTOOLCHAIN "v"` plus any tail therefore
   336	answered for a family no host produces — and answered `rejected`, which is
   337	exactly where a fabrication hides: for a value the isolated measurement already
   338	rejects, the fabricated verdict agrees, the crosscheck compares equal, and the
   339	row goes green. Recognition is therefore whole-line and exact against forms
   340	predicted before the command runs, and the rejection direction is neither safer
   341	nor less tested than the acceptance one.
   342	
   343	**Closure is measured rather than asserted.** The probe classifies outcomes
   344	deliberately outside the recognised set — real unrelated command failures, every
   345	measured outcome cross-fed against every other value, and measured diagnostics
   346	extended the way a later release extends a message — and requires each to yield
   347	no verdict, reporting for every fabrication which of the two laundering
