Verdict: **CHANGES REQUESTED**. Task routed from `reviewing` to `analysis`; no `commit_ack` supplied.

Four blocking findings:

- Fingerprint normalization rejects the multiline `rustc -vV` output it requires.
- The graph command lacks `--all-features`, contradicting its all-feature claim and vector 19. Cargo requires the explicit flag to activate every feature. [Cargo metadata](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-metadata.html)
- Outside-root path dependencies are rejected only after Cargo has read their manifests. Cargo permits paths such as `../dependency`. [Cargo path dependencies](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/specifying-dependencies.html#specifying-path-dependencies)
- The probe does not exercise the exact vendored, manager-configured pipeline or both source modes; Windows TOML path serialization is also unspecified.

Independent probe replay passed: 19/19 cases, P1/P2, 24 closure checks, 6/6 controls, and 8/8 structural checks. Curator Go tests and vet also passed.

